Training-image caveat, stated plainly: opencv_zoo issues 318 and 320 ask
whether the datasets used to train these checkpoints (WIDER FACE is a known
noncommercial set; the SFace training set is not named on the model card)
limit downstream use of the weights. The LICENSE files published next to the
ONNX files are MIT for YuNet and Apache-2.0 for SFace, and both of those
licenses allow commercial use of the files they cover. This project relies
on those published file licenses. It does not claim the training images
themselves are commercially licensed.

InsightFace is not bundled. Its pretrained weights are often limited to
noncommercial research use. Do not download them into this repository.
MATCHER_MODE=insightface remains an explicit sidecar opt-in.

Palantir and Flock Safety libraries and products are not bundled.
